# WARD 42 FIX-IT - SECURITY TEST REQUESTS
# Run with the REST Client extension in VS Code while Flask is running locally.
# Run one test at a time. Check the expected result in each heading.
# IMPORTANT: Do not commit real session cookies or CSRF tokens to source control.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000

### TEST 01 - Public report form - EXPECT 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/report

### TEST 02 - Protected coordinator panel - EXPECT redirect to /coordinator/login
# REST Client may follow the redirect and show the login page with 200 OK.
GET {{baseUrl}}/coordinator

### TEST 03 - Protected all-reports page - EXPECT redirect to login
GET {{baseUrl}}/coordinator/reports

### TEST 04 - Protected dashboard - EXPECT redirect to login
GET {{baseUrl}}/coordinator/dashboard

### TEST 05 - Unauthenticated JSON API - EXPECT 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/summary
Accept: application/json

### TEST 06 - Report submission without CSRF token - EXPECT 400 Bad Request
# This tests CSRF enforcement, NOT description validation.
POST {{baseUrl}}/report
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

category=Pothole&street=Test+Street&description=Test+report+with+enough+characters&reporter_name=Test+Resident&reporter_cell=0821234567

### TEST 07 - Login without CSRF token - EXPECT 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/coordinator/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=invalid_test_user&password=invalid_test_password

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADVANCED TESTS 08-10: REQUIRE A VALID CSRF TOKEN AND ITS MATCHING SESSION COOKIE.
# First open GET /report or GET /coordinator/login and obtain the current
# csrf_token form value and matching session cookie in the same browser session.
# Do NOT run these requests until those values have been set correctly.
# In the REST Client extension, a missing/wrong token will produce 400 and does
# not prove the intended SQL injection, XSS, or upload-validation check.
# Delete real values from this file after testing.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_VALID_CSRF_TOKEN
@sessionCookie = REPLACE_WITH_MATCHING_SESSION_COOKIE_VALUE

### TEST 08 - SQL injection attempt in coordinator login - EXPECT login REJECTED
# Valid CSRF + cookie required; the username must not bypass authentication.
# Expected login message: Invalid username or password.
POST {{baseUrl}}/coordinator/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Cookie: session={{sessionCookie}}

csrf_token={{csrfToken}}&username=%27+OR+1%3D1+--&password=definitely_wrong_password

### TEST 09 - XSS probe in report description - EXPECT safe rendering
# Valid CSRF + cookie required. Creates a TEST report if accepted.
# After submitting, inspect how its description appears on the coordinator page.
# It should appear as text, never execute JavaScript.
POST {{baseUrl}}/report
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Cookie: session={{sessionCookie}}

csrf_token={{csrfToken}}&category=Pothole&street=Security+Test+Street&description=%3Cscript%3Ealert%281%29%3C%2Fscript%3E&reporter_name=Security+Test&reporter_cell=0821234567

### TEST 10 - Invalid photo type - EXPECT 400 Bad Request
# Valid CSRF + cookie required; the TXT file must be rejected by save_photo().
POST {{baseUrl}}/report
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Ward42TestBoundary
Cookie: session={{sessionCookie}}

--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="csrf_token"

{{csrfToken}}
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

Pothole
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="street"

Security Test Street
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Testing invalid photo file rejection.
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="reporter_name"

Security Test
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="reporter_cell"

0821234567
--Ward42TestBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="not_an_image.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is not an image.
--Ward42TestBoundary--
